<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngola Hari</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ngola Ari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngola Hari was a ruler of Ndongo in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, installed by the Portuguese in 1626 as a rival to Queen Njinga. Based at the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pungo-andongo">Pungo Andongo</a>, he depended on Portuguese support while Njinga fought on from Matamba. When his successor rebelled, the Portuguese stormed Pungo Andongo in 1671, ending the kingdom of Ndongo.</p></div>
